  "instruction": "Open the Sales app (via the apps menu top-left). Create a new quotation: click New. In the Customer field, type 'fwod101-n1 Bench Customer' and select the matching option from the autocomplete dropdown that appears (the value only counts if chosen from the dropdown, not merely typed). Then in the Order Lines table, add exactly ONE order line: click into the Product field of the first line, type or search for any real product from the product catalogue (e.g. a product that exists in the dropdown list) and select it from the autocomplete dropdown. Set that line's Quantity to 3. Let the app fill the unit price automatically. Then save the quotation (click Save). Report: (a) the exact product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that line, (c) the Untaxed Amount the app computes (shown in the totals section), and (d) the quotation reference/name if one is shown. Do not confirm the order. Do not wait for network idle; wait for concrete page state.",
